== Draft lottery ==
{{further|NBA draft lottery}}
The first 14 picks in the draft belong to teams that missed the [[2012 NBA playoffs|playoffs]]; the order was determined through a lottery. The lottery was only used to determine the teams that obtained the first three picks in the draft. The remaining first-round picks and the second-round picks were assigned to teams in reverse order of their win–loss record in the [[2011–12 NBA season|previous season]].<ref name="DraftLotteryRules">{{Cite web |last=Golliver |first=Ben |date=May 30, 2012 |title=The 2012 NBA Draft Lottery: Anthony Davis Sweepstakes |url=https://www.cbssports.com/nba/news/the-2012-nba-draft-lottery-anthony-davis-sweepstakes/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180701012558/https://www.cbssports.com/nba/news/the-2012-nba-draft-lottery-anthony-davis-sweepstakes/ |archive-date=July 1, 2018 |access-date=September 8, 2023 |website=[[CBS Sports]]}}</ref> To determine the top three picks, fourteen ping pong balls numbered 1–14 were placed into a lottery machine. Four random balls were selected for each of the three picks and there were a total of 1,001 combinations. The lottery was weighted so that the teams with the worst records had better chances at the first pick. For example, the [[Charlotte Bobcats]] had the worst record from the previous season, so they were assigned 250 of the 1,001 combinations, which meant they had a 25% chance of getting the first pick.<ref name="DraftLotteryExplained">{{Cite web |date=September 16, 2015 |title=How does the NBA lottery system work? |url=https://sites.psu.edu/siowfa15/2015/09/16/how-does-the-nba-lottery-system-work/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231020175226/https://sites.psu.edu/siowfa15/2015/09/16/how-does-the-nba-lottery-system-work/ |archive-date=October 20, 2023 |access-date=October 20, 2023 |website=[[Pennsylvania State University]]}}</ref>

The lottery was held on May 30, 2012, in the [[Times Square Studios|Disney/ABC Times Square Studio]] in New York City.<ref>{{Cite web |date=May 29, 2012 |title=Bobcats hope to secure No. 1 pick |url=https://www.espn.com/nba/draft2012/story/_/id/7985631 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201020012957/https://www.espn.com/nba/draft2012/story/_/id/7985631 |archive-date=October 20, 2020 |access-date=October 18, 2020 |website=[[ESPN]]}}</ref> The [[New Orleans Hornets]] won the rights to the [[List of first overall NBA draft picks|first overall selection]] with a 13.7% chance to win. The Hornets were a league-owned team at the time, leading to continued [[NBA draft conspiracy|conspiracy theories about the lottery process]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Helin |first=Kurt |date=June 11, 2012 |title=David Stern expects your draft conspiracy theories now |url=https://www.nbcsports.com/nba/news/david-stern-expects-your-draft-conspiracy-theories-now |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230627174933/https://www.nbcsports.com/nba/news/david-stern-expects-your-draft-conspiracy-theories-now |archive-date=June 27, 2023 |access-date=June 27, 2023 |website=[[NBC Sports]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Dengate |first=Jeff |date=May 16, 2007 |title=Let the Ping-Pong Balls Fall |url=http://www.nba.com/features/inside_lottery_050524.html |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120523105241/http://www.nba.com/features/inside_lottery_050524.html |archive-date=May 23, 2012 |access-date=June 13, 2012 |website=[[NBA.com]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Schoenfield |first=David |date=June 29, 2009 |title=The first lottery draft still rates the best |url=https://www.espn.com/espn/page2/story?page=draftreview/090624 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121102185600/http://sports.espn.go.com/espn/page2/story?page=draftreview/090624 |archive-date=November 2, 2012 |website=[[ESPN]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=June 13, 2012 |title=David Stern, Jim Rome battle on radio |url=https://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/8048426/nba-commissioner-david-stern-radio-host-jim-rome-get-lottery |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120614053048/http://espn.go.com/nba/story/_/id/8048426/nba-commissioner-david-stern-radio-host-jim-rome-get-lottery |archive-date=June 14, 2012 |website=[[ESPN]]}}</ref> The Bobcats won the second overall pick despite having the highest odds to win the lottery.<ref name="DraftLotteryResults">{{Cite web |date=May 30, 2012 |title=Hornets win NBA draft lottery |url=https://www.espn.com/nba/draft2012/story/_/id/7989513/2012-nba-draft-new-orleans-hornets-win-draft-lottery-secure-no-1-overall-pick |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160819022923/https://www.espn.com/nba/draft2012/story/_/id/7989513/2012-nba-draft-new-orleans-hornets-win-draft-lottery-secure-no-1-overall-pick |archive-date=August 19, 2016 |access-date=September 8, 2023 |website=[[ESPN]]}}</ref>

